      "id": "FIN-01",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "anchor": "inputs-flag-incidence",
      "title": "The three arithmetic vertices and their residue flags",
      "statement": "Let Kᵣ=Dᵣ⁻¹SL_N(𝒪)Dᵣ for r=0,1,2, Eᵢⱼ=Kᵢ∩Kⱼ and B=K₀∩K₁∩K₂. In the basis at each vertex, its ordered pair (E,E′) stabilizes respectively a line in a plane, a line in a hyperplane, and a hyperplane containing a codimension-two space. The distinguished subgroup E has a single double coset outside itself, and the other stabilizer satisfies [E′:B]≥q for q=|𝒪/(π)|.",
      "hypotheses": "L′ a number field, π a prime element of its integer ring, N≥3, q≥25 at the selected callsite. The conclusion about finite incidence is arithmetic. Total complexity of L′ is used in the eventual archimedean Hecke comparison.",
      "definitions": [
