      "title": "The exact norm in the projective plane at residue size 25",
      "statement": "For N=3 and q=25 the normalized point-to-line incidence operator has norm 5/26 on the mean-zero subspace. Its action on the signed difference of two point masses has 25 entries +1/26, 25 entries −1/26 and zero elsewhere. The finite-group comparison gives the weaker bound 1/√26 in this instance, and the selected general argument uses 1/5.",
      "hypotheses": "Work at vertex 0 of the residue graph in a three-dimensional vector space over 𝔽₂₅, with uniform norms on each vertex type (their sizes coincide). This is a finite example of the link used by the estimate and does not identify its exact spectral value with that of the global Hecke operator.",
